    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0452" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/6–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Korea
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-03T19:00:00-04:00">June 3, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>417. In planning initiate activity contemplated under para 4(d) Res Dec 12,
                        1948<anchor n="1" xml:id="d258-f1"/>
                    UNCOK may wish through suitable channels
                    approach USSR with view verifying with assistance USSR military experts the
                    already announced withdrawal USSR occupation forces from north Korea,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d258-f2"/> simultaneously with UNCOK (and US military experts) observation and verification
                    withdrawal US occupation forces from ROK. There
                    is of course little hope response to such approach wld be affirmative, but
                        UNCOK might find step appropriate for
                    record with respect this para of Res, and as further endeavor obtain access
                    north Korea. Chairman UNCOK might ask UNSYG address both US and USSR regarding UNCOK desire undertake such verification
                    withdrawal occupation forces throughout Korea.</p>
                <p>If USSR shd in reply propose their military experts accompany UNCOK in observation and verification in ROK, assumed acceptance proposal wld be contingent
                    upon identical access for UNCOK and US
                    military experts throughout north Korea.</p>
                <p>If no objection, you may informally broach suggestion to appropriate UNCOK contacts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d258-f1" n="1" xml:id="d258-f1-content">
                <p>The paragraph under reference directed UNCOK to
                    “observe the actual withdrawal of the occupying forces and verify the fact of
                    withdrawal when such has occurred; and for this purpose, if it so desires,
                    request the assistance of military experts of the two occupying powers”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f2" n="2" xml:id="d258-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 10, <ref target="#pg950">p. 950</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
